+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="UTF-8">
+  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
+  <title>Privacy | The Daily Grind</title>
+  <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
+  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'none'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'none'; connect-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; require-trusted-types-for 'script'; trusted-types 'none'">
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/styles.css">
+</head>
+<body>
+  <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
+    <a class="logo" href="/">THE DAILY GRIND</a>
+    <a href="/">Back to home</a>
+  </nav>
+  <main class="container privacy-content">
+    <h1>Privacy, by default</h1>
+    <p>Last updated: October 23, 2026</p>
+    <p>This notice covers the Daily Grind informational pages. You can browse them without creating an account or providing personal details.</p>
+    <h2>What these pages collect</h2>
+    <p>These pages have no forms, analytics, advertising trackers, or client-side scripts. They do not set cookies, store information in your browser, request device permissions, or build a device fingerprint.</p>
+    <h2>Images and third parties</h2>
+    <p>Our coffee image and stylesheet are served from this website. Your browser does not need to contact an image provider, font service, or social media service to display these pages.</p>
+    <h2>Hosting and request information</h2>
+    <p>Delivering a page sends your IP address and ordinary request information to our hosting provider. The hosting service may keep access and security logs. Its retention and deletion settings depend on the deployment; these pages do not control those logs.</p>
+    <h2>Accounts, orders, and your choices</h2>
+    <p>This static website does not implement account creation, checkout, or account data storage. If those services are introduced, they will need a separate explanation of the information requested, its purpose, retention, and how to access, correct, or delete it before collecting data.</p>
+    <p>There are no optional trackers to accept or reject and no site-created browser data to delete. Hosting logs, if retained, must be managed by the website operator through the hosting provider.</p>
+    <p><a href="/">Return to The Daily Grind</a></p>
+  </main>
+  <footer><p>&copy; 2026 The Daily Grind Coffee Co. All rights reserved.</p></footer>
+</body>
+</html>
